        "dimension": "adherence",
        "findings": [
          {
            "dimension": "adherence",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/daemon/repo-convert.ts:43",
            "message": "A preview (the default mode of repo.convert) calls `planConversion(repoPath, { rules: CONVERSION_RULES })` without a tracker port, even when the repository has a GitHub tracker configured. The tracker is opened only on the apply path. So the preview never lists the pre-s8 'Attached ...' comments in `legacyAttachComments`, and it never plans the optional relabel either. The design makes preview the step where the user reads the legacy attach comments before applying. The s9 hand-off (docs/plans/core-data-model.md) also tells the owner to 'check the preview on the real repository with the tracker configured', but the preview as built cannot show them.",
            "expectationRef": "LLD planConversion options.tracker ('A tracker port, when the optional issue relabel and pre-s8 comment listing may be planned'); migration step 6 (the preview read covers 'legacy attach comments'); PLAN t11 ('when a tracker port is supplied list the pre-s8 attach comments in the plan and the report')"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dimension": "conventions",
        "findings": [
